ceace9aaf | RS","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"69862474-3af7-44ee-bb3c-1ff4f6103738","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:05.84519+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:05.860444+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":null,"pte_task_type":"REPEAT_SENTENCE","task_type_key":"REPEAT_SENTENCE","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":"5f24680b-71cc-4fff-8a03-5ffa9e872bff","image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"Do you think new developments in science often cause more problems than they solve?","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"72d38edc-5bb1-48b6-b7df-fae140e97c7a","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":33,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 DESCRIBE_IMAGE 4d40d66fd48d5047 | [MOCK] Nuclear Power Plants","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"69a63a8d-32cd-4e3d-99c1-021f89ca30ac","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:07.489137+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:07.499485+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":null,"pte_task_type":"DESCRIBE_IMAGE","task_type_key":"DESCRIBE_IMAGE","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":"f296c804-32e5-43d1-a606-7b4c5936565a","rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"The following graph gives information about nuclear power plants in operation in Europe.\nAs we can see from the map, the largest nuclear electricity generation is in France, which is 59.\nFollowing that the second largest one is found in Russia, and it is 30.\nIn contrast, the Netherlands has the smallest number, just 1.\nApart from that, Spain has 7, Germany has 8 and the United Kingdom has 15.\nTo sum up, the graph tells about how nuclear electricity generation is distributed in Europe.","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"a40b49df-894b-40e9-9e9d-81c09aaaaa03","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":34,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 DESCRIBE_IMAGE 7eb3819838675463 | [MOCK] World Water","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"a83bc591-2237-457b-9c3d-e42203f611d5","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:08.237435+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:08.253263+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":null,"pte_task_type":"DESCRIBE_IMAGE","task_type_key":"DESCRIBE_IMAGE","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":"6ce39f3e-a106-4670-836b-8a4e3fc7a08c","rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"The following graph gives information about the world's water distribution.\nIt can be seen that 97.5% of the world's water is salt water and only 2.5% is freshwater.\nIn the freshwater sector, glaciers and permanent snow occupy the largest proportion at 68.7%.\nAnd, groundwater occupies 30.06% of the fresh water.\nGround ice and permafrost takes up 0.86% of fresh water and other resources, 1.22%.\nIn the other sector, lakes occupy the majority of the percentage, about 0.26%.\nIn conclusion, this image gives information about the world's water distribution.","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"45f8fbcd-1f9e-4939-a3db-8963e44424dd","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":35,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 DESCRIBE_IMAGE 7650a22dff354654 | [MOCK] Adult Literacy","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"d44d2de4-8e8b-474f-9e99-54f4919f258a","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:09.374769+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:09.386331+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":null,"pte_task_type":"DESCRIBE_IMAGE","task_type_key":"DESCRIBE_IMAGE","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":"b3f7dbb5-66bd-4854-96f7-1837194a54c7","rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"The following graph gives information about adult literacy by region from 2000-2004.\nAs we can see the largest amount is in Latin America and the Caribbean, 89% in females and 91% in males.\nAnd Asia has the second highest rate, 73% in females and 86% in males.\nHowever, we can see the smallest amounts in sub-Saharan Africa, which are 53% in females and 70% in males.\nIn conclusion, males have a larger adult literacy rate than females in all the regions.","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"90fda1eb-a5b0-461a-8e14-2e0207c452be","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":36,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 DESCRIBE_IMAGE 86c0994381366d47 | [MOCK] Sport Participants","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"6e165771-1d38-44fd-856a-ea0338f49778","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:10.461746+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:10.473199+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":null,"pte_task_type":"DESCRIBE_IMAGE","task_type_key":"DESCRIBE_IMAGE","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":"bfa27e5f-affd-4f18-a1ec-97dfb875359b","rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"The bar chart shows the percentages of male and female participants in four sports.\nFootball has the highest percentage of male participants, at 70%, but only 30% for females.\nThe figures for cricket are 60% and 40%, while basketball records 55% and 45%.\nIn tennis, the female proportion was higher, about 60%, compared with 40% for males.\nOverall, football shows the largest gender difference.\nTo sum up, males participate more in football, cricket and basketball, while females participated more in tennis.","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"e3eb494d-2e18-4fe6-97be-872be8c80ae0","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":37,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 RE_TELL_LECTURE a468e68edeae08bc | Gas Giants","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"2156fc04-502e-4dd6-80ad-0f13be763f11","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:11.820294+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:11.83137+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":null,"pte_task_type":"RE_TELL_LECTURE","task_type_key":"RE_TELL_LECTURE","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":"92666322-bfdc-4275-b0dc-46bbf9e9d559","image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"So there are two theories for how the gas giants formed. One is the same theory I showed you just now core accretion, right. And the other is called disk instability and one of our colleagues at DTM has done a lot of work on that and so it's unclear exactly how they formed but you're right what we're trying to do the reason we're trying to get the higher and higher pressure in the lab is because we are trying to understand more about the pressure inside the gas giants. It's thought that the gas giants also have a metallic core, but maybe the metallic core not made of iron. Hydrogen, for example becomes metallic at a certain pressure. So it's very possible that the insides of these planets could have metallic cores, could have hydrogen cores, could have rocky portions we're not sure. But the higher pressure we can get in the lab, the closer we can get understanding the interiors of the gas giants and the exoplanet that are so big.","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"523cb72b-3251-4911-8a7a-ae8ad2b7389c","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":38,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 RE_TELL_LECTURE 4c866a81eeea4727 | RL","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"575d6615-d72c-4f38-8cb8-c03305e1d0cc","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:12.829871+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:12.840791+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":null,"pte_task_type":"RE_TELL_LECTURE","task_type_key":"RE_TELL_LECTURE","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":"e9598b12-1ca3-43e5-88c4-6e25da77c46b","image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"Hello everyone. Today's lecture is about setting up a website. I'm going to be focusing on things that you need to consider to ensure your website really adds value to the people using it.\nSo - there are three main areas you need to think about. The first and most important thing is who is your target audience? When you're creating a new website you really need to think about who the users are and what\ninformation they'll be looking for. What we do when we set up websites is to group users based on their needs. So, for a website in the academic community, for example, we may have groups such as researchers and administrators, and this helps us design the site and add information that is relevant to each group.\nThe second point is accessibility. The main thing here is to ensure your website can be found. And you can do this by making sure it can be reached from areas on the web where your target audience are also active. So this may mean providing links on other websites or maybe using social media.\nAnd thirdly - retention-making sure your target audience return to your website regularly. You do this by ensuring it gives them a reason to come back. So it's important to keep the site up-to-date and make sure it provides the latest news and interesting information and so on.","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"ac11020f-7749-48f3-9081-9aa3fae3d2a7","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":39,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 RE_TELL_LECTURE e520c9870f0a1e43 | Super-symmetry","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"5a8c4747-5192-49e7-840a-f03f56e41c98","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:14.317096+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:14.331747+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":null,"pte_task_type":"RE_TELL_LECTURE","task_type_key":"RE_TELL_LECTURE","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":"0ada5492-dcab-4551-a7cb-e49d6cbc1acd","image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"Super-symmetry is a mathematical idea that people have developed an effort to understand the sharpest organising principle for the fundamental constituents of matter. You see, we have learned that particles that seem to be different, can actually secretly be united by certain symmetry principles. So we use the fact that there are symmetric objects in the world like a sphere or basketball. You turn a sphere, and even though you've transformed it, it looks the same fundamentally. We found that certain particles when you transform one particle into another, even though looks like the identity of the particle has changed, overall the equations describing it they don't change at all at an underlying level of symmetry, but we've not been able to do is find a symmetry that would relate certain kinds of particles, namely matter particles and force particles. Matter particles are particles like electrons, muons and quarks, force particles are like photons and gluons and WZ bosons. Super-symmetry is a symmetry that actually relates to these two kinds, these two classes of particles. And people have proven that super-symmetry is the last possible symmetry of the fundamental particles that are mathematics, reality has not yet been shown to make use of it. So people are now trying to see whether that symmetry might actually be working in the world can be found evidence for it in our understanding of fundamental particles.","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"16b0d895-d27c-4373-8a84-524531bbdd01","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":40,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION 4ee6410997b3208e | ASQ","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"978188ff-02f8-4b9b-8c8a-31c875a4c62f","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:15.301401+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:15.314488+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"What is the word for the place where a river starts?","pte_task_type":"ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION","task_type_key":"ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":"bc9d7e3f-2806-444d-8c37-0985a1a939ed","image_prompt_re