:"ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":"11abd5c2-718c-4fe5-ba96-5603d871f2f6","image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":"Wrist watch / watch","supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":null,"available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"318868d2-f673-4cc1-b66c-a95babdd7447","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":45,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION beb5730bd8a9327f | ASQ","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"89ecbc83-28d7-4611-beb4-aa6dfbb0eb91","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:19.936818+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:19.948046+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"What do we call the list of steps that tell you how to put something together?","pte_task_type":"ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION","task_type_key":"ANSWER_SHORT_QUESTION","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":"ad762dd4-4876-4c37-bd57-80636e007f08","image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":"Instructions / directions / specifications / manual","supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":null,"available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"5557c3b1-5b65-4caa-9b48-169aa1a918b1","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":46,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION fa1ff5bf92a3bed8 | [MOCK] Eco-tourism","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"4ed21e71-2847-4d36-80cc-ce8f449c5a62","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:21.164896+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:21.173982+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"The speakers discuss the growing trend towards eco-tourism holidays and whether they really protect the environment and local cultures.","pte_task_type":"SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION","task_type_key":"SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":"93f16e83-eba4-4237-8b56-130b6be25dcb","image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"This lecture mainly talks about eco-tourism holidays. Firstly, the speaker emphasizes nowadays there is an increasing trend towards eco-tourism holidays. Also, he mentions the tourism should not only protect but also actively improve our environment and its cultures. Lastly, the speaker believes travelers can make the right choice when confronted with this type of marketing. In conclusion, this lecture is very informative.","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"e0ad0ee5-3013-41e0-8294-61d9db88e626","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":47,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION 0ce4a5f064cfb118 | [MOCK] Climate Change","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"e25d018d-dcac-4ff2-901d-511ca3a6c224","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:22.406227+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:22.418037+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"The speakers discuss the evidence that climate change is the result of human activities since the industrial revolution.","pte_task_type":"SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION","task_type_key":"SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":"7498a956-b96e-409e-ab32-0e7a9dfd0e07","image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"Climate change is a result of human activities, as our own actions are causing a genuine threat. To be more specific, land and sea temperatures started to increase around 200 years ago, when the industrial revolution began. This has resulted in the production of harmful gases, which is the proof of the damaging effect of our actions.","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"a62051b5-8697-426d-bcd0-cd1544944519","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":48,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION f441ab2f47600db9 | [MOCK] Allergies","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"58a21bae-c28c-4844-b9bb-2c8fb733bc04","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:23.369195+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:23.379479+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"The speakers discuss why allergies are becoming more common and how people who suffer from them can be treated.","pte_task_type":"SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION","task_type_key":"SUMMARIZE_GROUP_DISCUSSION","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":"e3570e93-c39b-45ed-8851-96f93e762670","image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"Allergies seem to be increasing these days especially in more hygienic societies where children are less exposed to harmful situations at an early age. They are a result of the body's immune system reacting to something it believes is harmful and producing histamines to get rid the body of this. Sufferers are advised to avoid the trigger for their allergy. When this is impossible, they can be prescribed anti-histamines.","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"12fdc9b6-f37d-457c-b3ef-bdd39e0e8212","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":49,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION 6eeb20bcd0636e18 | Shared Study Space","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"c297777a-2b55-47f9-a42c-a58e7f625614","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:24.357783+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:24.369138+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"You manage a small local library and have arranged a space within it for community members to study and work. Upon a routine check, you find that the area is cluttered with personal items left behind. You need to address this issue with the community members. What would you say to the community members?","pte_task_type":"RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION","task_type_key":"RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":"f04eab73-566e-4f02-a8a4-4bea48034fa6","image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"I wanted to talk about the condition of our shared study space in the library. This area is a valuable resource for our community. To maintain its usefulness and ensure it remains welcoming for everyone, I kindly ask that you please clean up after yourselves, respect the furniture, and keep the space tidy. Your cooperation is greatly appreciated in keeping our library a conducive place for learning and collaboration. Thank you for your understanding and help.","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"7820088f-c8bd-4329-b394-29e339650951","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":50,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION 875352ef33ff064d | Deadline Extension","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"408ed319-0f58-42cf-8444-913e684d185b","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:25.568578+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:25.5786+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"During a team meeting on Tuesday, your supervisor asks if you can complete and submit a comprehensive project update for a client by Friday. However, you're waiting on essential feedback from a key team member who's out of the office until Thursday. What would you say to your supervisor?","pte_task_type":"RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION","task_type_key":"RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":"79df8377-11d0-43ff-b205-368db17f25e2","image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"Actually, I might need a bit more time to get that project update ready for the client. The thing is, I'm waiting on some important feedback from one of our team members who's out until Thursday. It's really cutting it close for me to compile everything and make sure it's all good by Friday. I was hoping we could maybe push the deadline to Monday? This way, I can make sure everything's on point. Really appreciate your understanding on this!","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"e5694e5e-8444-4ce2-9bc2-d05f3d78bf04","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":51,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION 335eaffa8a33f9ab | A Spa Day","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"4c51bd3a-81ff-4b2f-8321-a9f91ccfeda5","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.57321+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.584735+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"You book a spa day based on glowing reviews and a wide range of services listed online. When you arrive, half the services are unavailable, and the facilities are not as advertised. How do you address this with the spa manager?","pte_task_type":"RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION","task_type_key":"RESPOND_TO_A_SITUATION","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":"a9ee82f7-32c4-4a93-bea2-28ff03463426","image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"SPEAKING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"It was quite a letdown to see many services aren't available and the facilities aren't as great as I expected. I was looking forward to the full experience. To make up for this gap between what was advertised and what's provided, could we maybe work out a partial refund or perhaps a voucher for a future visit when all services are back? I think that'd be a fair way to ensure I still get the relaxing experience I was excited about.","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"a86927f3-68b3-4081-b9f6-4f2cd55d3b4e","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":52,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT b8ce3c2e7d13f9f2 | 2014 Olympics","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"694a456d-db80-4a88-bc6b-9f6f94e9fee9","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.601369+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.611428+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"11 February 2009 – Major athletic events around the globe – from the 2014 Sochi Olympics to an annual powerboat race in Norwegian fjords – are striving to neutralize their carbon footprint as part of a world-wide climate network, the United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP) said today.\nThe sporting events are the latest participants to join the network, and are particularly important for inspiring further global action on the environment, said Achim Steiner, UNEP Executive Director.\n\"It is, therefore, heartening that this passion for excellence increasingly encompasses environmental performance, with sporting organizations raising the bar ever higher at each and every tournament,\" he added.\nOrganizers of the 2014 Sochi Olympic and Paralympic Winter Games – to be held in a unique natural setting between the shores of the Black Sea and the soaring snow-capped Caucasus Mountains – say they will put an estimated $1.75 billion into energy conservation and renewable energy.\nThat investment will be dedicated to improving transport infrastructure and offsetting greenhouse gas emissions from the use of electricity, air travel and ground transportation, the reforestation of Sochi National Park and the development of green belts in the city.","pte_task_type":"SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT","task_type_key":"SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":75,"min_word_count":5,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"WRITING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"Major athletic events around the globe are striving to neutralize their carbon footprint as part of a world-wide climate network, which are the latest participants to join the network, and are particularly important for inspiring further global action on the environment, so this passion for excellence increasingly encompasses environmental performance, and that investment will be dedicated to improving transport infrastructure and offsetting greenhouse gas emissions.","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"9ea3de0d-0aec-4ed2-9fae-1f2202361867","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":53,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT 34f3013ec36e41b9 | 3D Printing","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"fe7c10f6-3b87-4ff7-8e50-b2a17b0cb630","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.62448+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.636437+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"Madeline Gannon is a researcher, teacher at the Carnegie Mellon University School of Architecture and Ph.D. candidate in Computational Design — but that’s not all. She is on a mission to open up the infinite design possibilities of 3D printing to the world. “Currently you have to have a lot of technical background in order to participate in creating things for 3D printers,” Gannon says. “There is still a huge knowledge barrier for how we create digital models.” As the technology has advanced, prices have plummeted, and now anyone can buy a 3D printer for a few hundred dollars, Gannon notes. However, not just anyone can create original designs for 3D-printed artifacts. To put true creative power into the hands of any ordinary 3D printer owner, Gannon has developed an innovative new system called 'Tactum'. Tactum is a new type of software that lets users create their own unique designs for 3D printers by simply touching a projected image. Using their innate hand gestures, someone using Tactum can poke, rub and otherwise manipulate the projected image that will become their 3D printed object, and see it instantly change shape in response. In keeping with the goal of democratizing the process, Gannon designed her first series of Tactum artifacts on a surface that everyone can access freely and manipulate instinctively, that being the human body.\n“My goal was to bring the digital out to the physical world and out onto your body,” says Gannon.\nAlong with a companion project called Reverb — which translates these user-created designs into printable meshes — that impulse has resulted in a spectacular diversity of bracelet and necklace designs, ranging from smooth landscapes, intricate textures and chaotic free forms to delicate geometries derived from the 19th century art of chronography.","pte_task_type":"SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT","task_type_key":"SUMMARIZE_WRITTEN_TEXT","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":75,"min_word_count":5,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"WRITING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":"Madeline Gannon is on a mission to open up the infinite design possibilities of 3D printing to the world, who has developed an innovative new system called 'Tactum', which lets users create their own unique designs for 3D printers, and Gannon designed her first series of Tactum artifacts on a surface that everyone can access freely and manipulate instinctively, which has resulted in a spectacular diversity of bracelet and necklace designs.","available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"e6dbcf4e-89b1-403e-a30a-f7c2c7dec85e","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":54,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 WRITE_ESSAY 43cef331df3475b9 | Einstein","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"61647b8d-9f99-4f7a-be1e-36cfae572389","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.653055+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.663874+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"“The only thing that interferes with my learning is education.” – Albert Einstein. What did he mean by that? Do you think he is correct?","pte_task_type":"WRITE_ESSAY","task_type_key":"WRITE_ESSAY","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":300,"min_word_count":200,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"WRITING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":null,"supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":null,"available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"0f40363b-415e-4fbe-9d50-d5b31bf003e2","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":55,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN fafe357a9a98f7b0 | Honorary Degree","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"962a4329-d706-4259-a6c3-4ecac00b4116","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.709795+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.724918+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"Victoria University of Wellington has conferred an honorary degree on a distinguished astrophysicist in a recent graduation ceremony. Professor Warrick Couch {{0}} the honorary degree of Doctor of Science for his remarkable contribution to our knowledge of galaxies and dark energy. Professor Couch is a distinguished astrophysicist who has {{1}} a crucial role in the discovery that the Universe is expanding at an accelerating rate, a finding which led to the lead scientists being awarded a Nobel Prize in Physics in 2011, which he attended in recognition of his contribution.\nIn his research, Professor Couch uses large ground-based and space-based telescopes to observe galaxy clusters, {{2}} are the largest Structures in the Universe. He is also involved in a number of national and international committees overseeing the management of these telescopes. {{3}} his own research activities, Professor Couch has worked to support young researchers and provide public comment on astronomy internationally.","pte_task_type":"FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN","task_type_key":"FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"READING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":"1.received, 2.played, 3.which, 4.In addition to","supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":null,"available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"70bd1bc9-7048-4909-b5ee-bbbc4801807b","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":56,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN 200184230430a6da | Keith Haring","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"3b042f0d-577f-4881-ae08-6bc3a34b5971","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.735927+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.748654+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"Keith Haring began as an underground artist, literally. His first famous projects were pieces of stylized graffiti {{1}} in New York subway stations. Haring travelled from station to station, drawing with chalk and chatting with commuters about his work. These doodles helped him develop his classic style and he grew so {{2}} , doing up to 40 drawings a day, that it was not long before fame and a measure of fortune followed.\nSoon, galleries and collectors from the art establishment wanted to buy full-sized pieces by Haring. The paintings skyrocketed in price but this did not sit well with Haring's philosophy. He believed that art, or {{3}} his art, was for everyone. Soon, Haring opened a store which he called the Pop Shop, which he hoped would attract a broad range of people. While somewhat controversial among street artists, some of {{4}} accused Haring of 'selling out', the Pop Shop changed the way people thought about the relationship between art and business.","pte_task_type":"FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN","task_type_key":"FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"READING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":"1.drawn, 2.prolific, 3.at least, 4.whom","supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":null,"available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"4fed0f51-dfaf-4fd0-a228-dc2b0d87f4ea","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":57,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN a26b6b029a5d1799 | Intelligence Comparison","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"a0741492-2bb3-44f7-9105-1aa8c55ccce1","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.762857+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.77595+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"Comparing the intelligence of animals of different species is difficult, how do you compare a dolphin and a horse? Psychologists have a technique for looking at intelligence that {{1}} not require the cooperation of the animal involved. The relative size of an individual's brain is a reasonable indication of intelligence. Comparing {{2}} species is not as simple as generally expected. An elephant will have a larger brain than a human has simply because it is a large beast. {{3}} , we use the Cephalization index, which compares the size of an animal's brain with the size of its body. Based on the Cephalization index, the brightest animals on the planet are humans, {{4}} by great apes, porpoises and elephants. As a general {{5}} , animals that hunt for a living (like canines) are smarter than strict vegetarians (you don't need much intelligence to outsmart a leaf of lettuce). Animals that live in social groups are always smarter and have larger EQ's than solitary animals.","pte_task_type":"FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN","task_type_key":"FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"READING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":"1.does, 2.across, 3.Instead, 4.followed, 5.rule","supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":null,"available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"f1e3422a-8132-4559-a5dc-6ec491032f1f","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":58,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN f803ff4baa97369e | Longevity","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"00c0c108-0b28-4d8b-baec-ebb2311b75c3","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.789384+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.803834+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"People are living longer and this longevity is good news for sales teams. It results in a much more {{1}} customer base for them to work from. Why we are living longer is not the issue for anyone {{2}} in drawing up plans to market a product. What they focus on is the fact that there are now more age groups to target, which means that a sales pitch can be re-worked a number of times to more exactly fit each one. For example, {{3}} referring simply to 'adults', there are now 'starting adults', 'young adults' and 'established adults'. {{4}} , markets no longer talk about 'children', but tend to refer to a fuller range of categories that includes 'kids', 'tweens', 'pre-teens' and 'teenagers'. We now have a very diverse population in terms of age, and that can only be a {{5}} for business.","pte_task_type":"FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN","task_type_key":"FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"READING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":"1.precise, 2.involved, 3.rather than, 4.Similarly, 5.bonus","supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":null,"available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"4a38d426-9171-4ab6-ac25-33f5111027ba","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":59,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN af800fc575682ca1 | Push and Pull","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"cd3454ce-7b30-485f-8e77-56f1dd7785ba","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.81747+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.834517+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"People move to a new region for many different reasons. The {{1}} for moving can come from a combination of what researchers sometimes call 'push and pull {{2}} ' — those that encourage people to leave a region, and those that attract people to a region. Some of the factors that motivate people to move {{3}} seeking a better climate, finding more affordable housing, looking for work or retiring from work, leaving the {{4}} of city living, wanting a more pleasant environment, and wanting to be near to family and friends. In reality, many complex factors and personal reasons may {{5}} to motivate a person or family to move.","pte_task_type":"FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN","task_type_key":"FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"READING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":"1.motivation, 2.factors, 3.include, 4.congestion, 5.interact","supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":null,"available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"67b66b32-5c90-4323-80b8-10952e47bf70","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":60,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN c60abdb5cef3a8e7 | Language Extinct","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"3998fd72-ecdb-4af3-96e4-24c8799226fc","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.847192+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.863415+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"At the moment, there are between six and seven thousand languages in the world. According to linguists, fifty percent of these are in danger {{1}} extinct. The speed of language loss has accelerated over the past few decades because businesses that need to communicate with a range of people from other cultures {{2}} to employ more widely used languages, such as English, Chinese, or Spanish. This attitude is understandable, but it means that many local languages are dying out before anyone {{3}} the opportunity to study them. According to linguists, some of these languages could reveal a great {{4}} of useful information about language learning and cognitive development. In addition, a local language that has been built on the local culture contains words and phrases that express that culture; lose the language and you arguably may lose the culture, too. And finally, historians will {{5}} that a language contains evidence of a region's history and should, for that reason alone, be preserved.","pte_task_type":"FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN","task_type_key":"FILL_IN_THE_BLANKS_DROPDOWN","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"READING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":"1.of becoming, 2.prefer, 3.has had, 4.deal, 5.argue","supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":null,"available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"c84e32c5-d672-4565-a3f1-5b181f57dc31","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":61,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 MC_READING_MULTIPLE 414bac31d3d978d9 | Wooden Sculptures","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"e278486a-39b5-4bc2-8148-2a9c26c675f0","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.877934+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.892861+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"Much has been written on the wooden sculptures of West Africa. Especially Nigeria, which was pre-eminent in the art, for unlike other crafts, wood-carving has long been acknowledged in the West as an art form.\nYet, compared with stone or bronze, wood is not a very durable material in tropical conditions and the oldest carvings in Nigeria are probably no more than two hundred and fifty years old. Many of the earliest. maybe the finest of the wood carvings may also have been destroyed by termites. When one is attacked in this way, no attempt is made to preserve it; a new one is made to replace it, for the creativity of making it is valued above the object per se. The finest sculptures were made for religious or ceremonial purposes, and the art of creation was itself a religious act.\n\nWhat has led to there being no very old wood carvings in West Africa?","pte_task_type":"MC_READING_MULTIPLE","task_type_key":"MC_READING_MULTIPLE","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"READING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":"the nature of the climate there\nproblems caused by insects","supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":null,"available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"0ea83766-9861-4002-8382-fba0ce143631","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":62,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 MC_READING_MULTIPLE b8964599c8eb161c | MCM-R","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"4c8578fe-dd9d-46b9-9c22-f4ca57cc19c9","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.905276+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.91609+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"It is possible to study the curriculum of an educational institution from a number of different perspectives. In the first instance, we can look at curriculum planning, that is at decision-making, in relation to identifying learners' needs and purposes; establishing goals and objectives; selecting and grading content; organising appropriate learning arrangements and learner groupings; selecting, adapting or developing appropriate materials, learning tasks and assessment and evaluation tools.\nAlternatively, we can study the curriculum 'in action', as it were. This second perspective takes us into the classroom itself. Here, we can observe the teaching/learning process and study the ways in which the intentions of the curriculum planners, which were developed during the planning phase, are put into action.\nYet another perspective relates to assessment and evaluation. From this perspective we would try and find out what students had learned and what they had failed to learn, in relation to what had been planned. In addition we might want to find out if they had learned anything which had not been planned.\n\nWhich of these ways of looking at an institution's curriculum is outlined in the text?","pte_task_type":"MC_READING_MULTIPLE","task_type_key":"MC_READING_MULTIPLE","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"READING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":"observing what happens during lessons\nconsidering what is taken into account when preparing the curriculum","supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":null,"available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"b811b4ef-61d7-469b-bf2a-a40e5914bcdb","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":63,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 MC_READING_MULTIPLE 11554f8b56406126 | Old Man of Lake","status":"APPROVED","deleted":false,"version":1,"public_id":"1cb7ae6f-06dd-4887-a0b2-a14ae62be076","tenant_id":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.928896+00:00","is_current":true,"updated_at":"2026-10-28T16:07:26.942433+00:00","visibility":"SHARED","prompt_text":"Small, localized enterprises are becoming ever-more imaginative in identifying opportunities to boost tourism for their areas. A more unusual attraction is the Old Man of the Lake, which is the name given to a 9-meter-tall tree stump that has been bobbing vertically in Oregon's Crater Lake since at least 1896. For over one hundred years, it has been largely ignored but recently it has become a must-see item on the list of lake attractions. Since January 2012, tour boats regularly include the Old Man on their sightseeing trips around the lake.\nAt the waterline, the stump is about 60 centimeters in diameter, and the exposed part stands approximately 120 centimeters above the surface of the water. Over the years, the stump has been bleached white by the elements. The exposed end of the floating tree is splintered and worn but wide and buoyant enough to support a person's weight.\nObservations indicated that the Old Man of Crater Lake travels quite extensively, and sometimes with surprising rapidity. Since it can be seen virtually anywhere on the lake, boat pilots commonly communicate its position to each other as a general matter of safety.\n\nWhich of the following are true of the Old Man of the Lake according to the text?","pte_task_type":"MC_READING_MULTIPLE","task_type_key":"MC_READING_MULTIPLE","ever_published":true,"max_word_count":null,"min_word_count":null,"revision_number":1,"audio_prompt_ref":null,"image_prompt_ref":null,"rejection_reason":null,"task_type_section":"READING","available_for_exam":true,"correct_answer_text":"It is a drifting piece of wood.\nIt can quickly move about the lake.\nIt can be a danger to boat users.","supersedes_public_id":null,"author_user_public_id":"cc916708-5818-45ad-a707-c34482f5fd97","reference_answer_text":null,"available_for_practice":false,"revision_group_public_id":"bce0c601-09ca-45c4-a893-31bd5b4ddc92","availability_flags_explicit":true},{"id":64,"pool":"EXAM","title":"DOC22 RE_ORDER_PARAGR